Until document is completed, use '\qtwopages \shipout\vbox{}' instead of '\quire{...}'

=======================================================================================
DESIGN DECISIONS:

In formats based on тех.tex, \\ is a dedicated control sequence
(in contrast to plain.tex).

For strut-based code (including tables) use uppercase font commands (e.g., TENRM).
(In \headline also use uppercase font commands, because \makeheadline uses
8.5pt, which is the height of a strut.)

After being built, TeX and MF must be configured by running 'make' in mytex/ (done
automatically).

PK fonts are generated using MakePK in mytex/dvips

MakePK generates pk files for ./ fonts on each run, because mf mode in current
run may be different from mf mode in previous run (tex- vs. tex+, dvi- vs. dvi+)
and there is no way to tell which mf mode was used for a given pk-file. Also, if
you are editing a character, you want to see new version of it on each run.

Start mf file with %! line if you need to set geometry, for example:
  %! pdfpagewidth=210mm pdfpageheight=297mm pdfhorigin=4.1mm pdfvorigin=20mm

Use \pdfhorigin and \pdfvorigin to set margins, \pdfpagewidth and \pdfpageheight to
set paper size.
(\pdfpagewidth, \pdfpageheight, \pdfhorigin and \pdfvorigin are stored in
comment of dvi file and are subsequently used as arguments to dvips.)
Default \pdfhorigin and \pdfvorigin for letter paper are 1in; to use default \hsize
and \vsize for a4 paper they are changed as follows:
  (210-6.5*25.4)/2=22.45mm
  (297-9*25.4)/2=34.2mm

PS is used instead of PDF because PS format allows to split document into pages,
leaving the rest of the document intact. And page splitting is critical, because
we can not generate only necessary pages in dvi-processing stage - we need to
actually see all the pages to be able to choose which pages to print, which
means that we must generate the whole document and open it in viewer - page
splitting will be done at a later stage by viewer.

For printing use only viewer which uses lpr program for printing (there are
viewers that connect to cups socket directly). This allows to override lpr with
ad-hoc program which sends the PS data directly to printer (after wrapping it in
PJL commands).
